From aea701aab9e74f93a1ebb9cb7e0745a0e0a58979 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 08:36:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 221/226] harden SNMP to v3-only + present SFTP as the default
 file-transfer method

Stage 1 (SNMP): lock out SNMPv1/v2c and require authenticated SNMPv3.
- rc/snmpd.c: stop emitting rocommunity/rwcommunity (v1/v2c send the community
  in cleartext with no auth); drop the noAuthNoPriv v3 path so the daemon
  refuses to create an unauthenticated user. Weak/empty passphrases already
  fail closed (net-snmp USM requires >= 8 chars).
- shared/defaults.c: default v3_auth_type=SHA, v3_priv_type=AES.
- www/Advanced_SNMP_Content.asp: remove the Get/Set Community fields and the
  NONE auth option; add a v3-only note. Priv NONE (auth-only) kept as advanced.

Stage 2 (SFTP UI + path): present SFTP as the preferred alternative to FTP.
- www/Advanced_AiDisk_ftp.asp: add a File transfer method selector with SFTP
  pre-selected (FTP only when already enabled); choosing SFTP hides the FTP
  config and links to Administration > System > SSH. No auto-SSH.
- dropbear/localoptions.h: point the SFTP subsystem at the in-image
  /usr/libexec/sftp-server (was the /opt Entware mount). The sftp-server
  binary is a follow-up; until then SFTP is non-functional as before (no regression).

Verified: make rt-be96u (as reaper) MAKE_EXIT=0, image built.
Follow-ups: openssh-sftp binary package, net-snmp 5.7.2 -> 5.9.x bump.
